// alpha reads its arguments and environment (env) and unit files and
// directories (fs); it starts services: it forks, execs, signals and polls
// its children (exec), and std.process reaches std.net (net), as the
// control socket will; and it crosses a small C membrane, src/sys/, for the
// steps of a start wolf has no call for yet (ffi, and unsafe for the raw
// memory those calls take). tools/check-membrane counts that membrane's
// declarations, and the number only falls.
pkg {
    name: "alpha",
    version: "0.0.0",
    edition: "1",
    capabilities: [env, fs, exec, net, ffi, unsafe],
}
